email.task:
You are an IT support technician. Sophie, a trainee in the HR department, needs to back up her work files to an external hard drive but does not know how. Write an email to Sophie explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- imperatives with sequence words;
- at least one softener (could you…?, just);
- at least one sentence with two objects (plug … into …, unplug … from …);
- at least one reason or purpose (to…, so that…, because…).
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
